VALUES
    -- ── George Orwell ──────────────────────────────────────
    (
        'Nineteen Eighty-Four', NULL,
        'Winston Smith works for the Ministry of Truth in London, chief city of Airstrip One. '
        'Big Brother stares out from every poster, the Thought Police uncover every act of '
        'betrayal. When Winston finds love with Julia, he discovers that life does not have '
        'to be dull and deadening, and awakens to new possibilities.',
        'eng', 328,
        '823.912', 'PR6029.R8',
        'Secker & Warburg', 1949,
        NULL, NULL,
        '0451524934', '9780451524935', 'OL7353544M',
        'https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/olid/OL7353544M-L.jpg'
    ),
    (
        'Animal Farm', 'A Fairy Story',
        'A farm is taken over by its overworked, mistreated animals. With flaming idealism '
        'and stirring slogans, they set out to create a paradise of progress, justice, and '
        'equality. Thus the stage is set for one of the most telling satiric fables ever '
        'penned—a razor-edged fairy tale for grown-ups.',
        'eng', 112,
        '823.912', 'PR6029.R8',
        'Secker & Warburg', 1945,
        NULL, NULL,
        '0451526341', '9780451526342', 'OL7353543M',
        'https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/olid/OL7353543M-L.jpg'
    ),
    (
        'Homage to Catalonia', NULL,
        'George Orwell''s personal account of his experiences in the Spanish Civil War, '
        'fighting alongside the POUM militia against Franco''s Nationalists. A vivid '
        'firsthand account of the war and a penetrating look at the political divisions '
        'that plagued the Republican side.',
        'eng', 232,
        '946.081', 'DP269.2',
        'Secker & Warburg', 1938,
        NULL, NULL,
        '0156421178', '9780156421171', 'OL7353549M',
        'https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/olid/OL7353549M-L.jpg'
    ),

    -- ── J.R.R. Tolkien ────────────────────────────────────────────
    (
        'The Hobbit', 'or There and Back Again',
        'Bilbo Baggins is a hobbit who enjoys a comfortable, unambitious life, rarely '
        'travelling any farther than his pantry or cellar. But his contentment is '
        'disturbed when the wizard Gandalf and a company of dwarves arrive on his doorstep '
        'one day to whisk him away on an adventure.',
